---
title: "Data operations"
description: "Upsert, update, scroll, count, and delete Qdrant points with QQL."
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

## Upsert

Every point requires exactly one case-insensitive `id` key.

{% qqlExample title="Payload and named vectors" %}
UPSERT INTO docs VALUES {
  id: 1,
  title: 'QQL',
  text: 'Declarative vector retrieval',
  vector: {dense: [0.1, 0.2, 0.3]}
};
{% /qqlExample %}

To embed payload fields during execution, use an embedding modifier:

{% qqlExample title="Multiple embedding destinations" %}
UPSERT INTO articles VALUES {
  id: 'article-1',
  title: 'Planning hybrid retrieval',
  body: 'Dense and sparse candidate generation'
}
EMBED body INTO dense_body USING DENSE,
      title INTO sparse_title USING SPARSE;
{% /qqlExample %}

## Update and delete

{% qqlExample title="Mutations" %}
UPDATE docs SET PAYLOAD = {status: 'reviewed'} WHERE id = 42;
UPDATE docs SET VECTOR dense = [0.2, 0.3, 0.4] WHERE id = 42;
DELETE PAYLOAD draft_notes FROM docs WHERE status = 'published';
DELETE VECTOR dense FROM docs WHERE id = 42;
DELETE FROM docs WHERE status = 'expired';
{% /qqlExample %}

Destructive point operations require an explicit selector.

## Browse and count

{% qqlExample title="Operational reads" %}
SCROLL FROM docs
WHERE status = 'published'
WITH VECTOR false
LIMIT 100;

COUNT FROM docs WHERE status = 'published';
{% /qqlExample %}
